// Constructed: an M57 KDC_ERR_PREAUTH_REQUIRED error with the client name and realm of the AS request in the same flow filled in, since Suricata logs `<empty>` in all M57 Kerberos errors and the suricata-verify checks (MIT) contain no such complete record. The KDC asks every regular logon for preauthentication, so the error becomes an informational Preauth failure of Authentication.
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_suricata
}
suricata::ocsf::normalize
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(this))
drop_null_fields
